  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 102.29 Bog",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 102.29 “Bog” means a wetland distinguished by stunted evergreen trees and shrubs, peat deposits, poor drainage, highly acidic soil conditions, highly acidic water conditions, or any combination thereof, as determined using “Natural Communities of New Hampshire”, 2nd edition, published by UNH Cooperative Extension dated 2011, available as noted in Appendix B.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13106, eff 9-25-20; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 102.30)",
